notes: >
  Vendored instead of pip-installed because momentfm's published pins
  (numpy==1.25.2, transformers==4.33.3, huggingface-hub==0.24.0) conflict with
  this project's dependencies. Import paths were rewritten (momentfm.* ->
  relative imports within this package). Not used for its published
  pretrained checkpoints; this project trains MOMENT from a random
  initialization on GiftEvalPretrain.

  Two intentional deviations from upstream models/moment.py, both scoped to
  models/moment.py only (all other vendored files are byte-for-byte copies):

  1. Dropped the forecast/classify/detect_anomalies/reconstruct/
     short_forecast methods and the embed.py DataEmbedding/TokenEmbedding/
     TemporalEmbedding classes they depend on, since this project only uses
     the reconstruction (masked pretraining) and embed tasks. Unused
     surface area, not a behavior change to what remains.
  2. reconstruction() now also returns, via TimeseriesOutputs.metadata, the
     pre-denorm normalized decoder output and the RevIN mean/stdev buffers
     used for that forward pass. Upstream only returns the denormalized
     (original-space) reconstruction. moment_adapter.py needs the
     normalized-space prediction to compute the moment_normalized loss
     condition without re-deriving RevIN statistics or duplicating the
     forward pass; this is a strict addition to the return value, the
     forward computation itself (normalize -> patch -> encode -> head ->
     denormalize) is unchanged.
